The '''Psi Mesh''' is the peer-to-peer encrypted radio mesh for operators and [[Field Recorder]] units in the field. It carries [[Psi-Tech]] telemetry, threat-signature exchange, and operator state-sharing across a small team without depending on cellular or internet infrastructure. The Psi Mesh is the field substrate that the [[PsiNet]] and the [[Earth Intelligence Network]] connect into when uplink is available, and stands alone when it is not.

== Theoretical context (Dicke psion superradiance) ==

Coherent operator coordination through a mesh produces collective
[[Psion|psion]] emission whose rate scales as <math>N^2</math> for
single-mode Dicke superradiance and as <math>N^4</math> for two-step
phase-locked emission - the same superradiance theorem that underlies
the [[Resonant_Pipeline#Theoretical_context_(Dicke_psion_superradiance)|Resonant
Pipeline]] scaling. The mesh is, in this picture, the engineering
substrate for the phase-locking that makes the higher-order scaling
accessible.

