== Tiered topology (cell / cluster / federation) for [[Tho'ra Tech]] ==
The mesh is structured in three concentric tiers, each
with distinct connectivity characteristics:

* '''Tier 1 — Cell''' (1–6 operators). All-to-all connectivity. Local
  state-shared by direct biofeedback exchange ([[HelmKit_Mk2.5|Mk2.5]]
  paired sessions) and [[Psi_Scanner]] peer-telemetry. Latency
  budget: <100 ms. This is the framework's primary trust-graph unit.
* '''Tier 2 — Cluster''' (3–8 cells, typically 12–40 operators).
  Cell-lead-mediated. Each cell exposes a single ''public'' state
  vector (aggregate HRV-coherence, aggregate EEG-coherence,
  declared-availability) to its cluster peers. Latency budget:
  <1 s. Cross-cell intervention requests route at this tier.
* '''Tier 3 — Federation''' (multi-cluster). Federation-level
  aggregation by [[Resonant_Pipeline]] coordinators. Operates on
  cluster-aggregate state only; individual-operator state is
  '''never''' exposed at this tier. Latency budget: <10 s. The
  primary purpose of Tier 3 is FP-budget calibration across
  geographically diverse cells.

The tiered design is the mesh's primary
[[Adversary_Classes|adversary-class]] defense: a state-actor
adversary may compromise a cell (Tier 1) without thereby being able
to read or influence cluster-level (Tier 2) or federation-level
(Tier 3) state.

== Protocol stack (L0–L5) ==
The mesh runs a layered protocol stack drawn
loosely from OSI but specialized to biophysical and psi-coupled
substrates:

* '''L0 — Physical''' (operators, biofeedback hardware,
  [[Neural_Network_Hardware]] nodes, conventional networking gear).
* '''L1 — Biophysical link''' ([[HelmKit_Mk1.5|Mk1.5]]+ paced
  breathing + HRV coherence; the link-level invariant the mesh's
  upper layers can assume).
* '''L2 — Cell session''' ([[HelmKit_Mk2.0|Mk2.0]] session-container
  semantics; defines the cell's shared
  [[Resonant_Field|resonant-field]] envelope).
* '''L3 — Mesh routing''' (gauge-bundle layer described under
  [[PsiNet]]; resolves intervention-request routing across cells
  and clusters).
* '''L4 — Pipeline orchestration''' ([[Resonant_Pipeline]] semantics;
  detection-verification-intervention-closure cycle).
* '''L5 — Federation telemetry''' (FP-budget accounting; long-term
  Bayesian prior maintenance).

Each layer's failure mode is contained at its layer. L1
biophysical-link failure (e.g. operator below Mk1.5 threshold) does
not corrupt L3 routing; the routing layer simply marks the operator
as unavailable.

== Federation layer ==
The federation-level (Tier 3) layer is the mesh's
'''calibration backbone'''. It performs:

* '''Cross-cluster FP-budget aggregation''' — pooling closure-outcome
  telemetry across clusters to detect cluster-local calibration drift.
* '''Adversary-class threat-model updates''' — propagating cluster-
  level threat-observations into mesh-wide adversary-class priors.
* '''Doctrine versioning''' — the framework's
  [[Falsification_Criteria_for_Psionics|F-criterion]] graduation
  signals propagate at this tier.
* '''No individual-operator telemetry''' — by hard architectural
  rule, individual-operator state is not exposed above Tier 2.

The federation layer is deliberately '''thin'''. Most of the mesh's
substantive coordination happens at Tier 1 (cell) and Tier 2
(cluster); the federation exists to keep the lower tiers honest, not
to centralize authority.

